# Code owners.
#
# ADR-048 AC-17b. This file exists for ONE path, and for a specific reason.
#
# The control that matters in ADR-048's security model is that branch code
# never reaches the self hosted runner on the VPS. Branch protection gives that
# control no teeth on its own: a same repository pull request runs the workflow
# YAML from its OWN branch, and this repository requires zero approvals, so a
# pull request that added `runs-on: injishi-vps` to a `pull_request` triggered
# job would reach the production host before anybody merged it.
#
# Two things close that, and both are required because they act at different
# moments. `scripts/check-workflow-triggers.mjs` runs as the `workflow-guard`
# job and fails such a pull request BEFORE it can merge. The rule below makes a
# workflow file the one path in this repository that cannot change without an
# approval, which is what stops the guard itself from being edited away in the
# same change.
#
# For the rule to bite, "Require review from Code Owners" must be on for `main`
# in the repository's branch protection settings. Without that, GitHub treats
# this file as a suggestion.

# Everything that defines, or could disable, the pipeline.
/.github/                     @sshami
/.github/workflows/           @sshami
/.github/actions/             @sshami

# The scripts the workflows call. A check is only as trustworthy as the file it
# runs, so the guard, the manifest check and the ratchet are owned too.
/scripts/check-workflow-triggers.mjs   @sshami
/scripts/check-workspace-manifests.mjs @sshami
/scripts/lint-ratchet.mjs              @sshami
/scripts/workspace-members.mjs         @sshami
/scripts/ci-changes.mjs                @sshami
/scripts/ci-complete.mjs               @sshami
/.github/lint-baseline.json            @sshami

# What a deploy actually runs on the host.
/infra/docker/deploy-stack.sh  @sshami
/infra/docker/demo-nightly.sh  @sshami
